          {
            title: 'Timing & Pressure',
            subtitle: 'The psychological warfare',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'strategy-block',
                title: '⏰ The Ticking Clock',
                description: 'Your hand size is your potential penalty. The longer you wait, the more devastating a sudden Showdown becomes. This forces action and prevents stagnation.',
              },
              {
                type: 'list',
                style: 'unordered',
                items: [
                  {
                    text: '3 cards: Manageable risk',
                  },
                  {
                    text: '5 cards: Moderate danger',
                  },
                  {
                    text: '7+ cards: Disaster waiting to happen',
                  },
                ],
              },
              {
                type: 'strategy-block',
                title: '⚖️ Patience vs. Aggression',
                description: 'The central tension of CLAIM. Do you call a Showdown with a decent hand now, or wait for a perfect one and risk someone else ending the game first?',
              },
              {
                type: 'highlight',
                text: 'In CLAIM, the player who acts decisively often wins over the player who waits for perfection.',
                emphasis: true,
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'The Open Floor Strategy',
            subtitle: 'Blocking and vulnerability',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'strategy-block',
                title: '🚧 The Art of the Block',
                description: 'The rule that anyone can pick up a Floor Card makes declaring a suit a terrifying act of vulnerability. Once you declare Spades, every Spade that appears becomes a target for your opponents to steal.',
                example: {
                  type: 'example',
                  title: 'Scenario',
                  text: "You declare Spades. The A♠ appears on the Floor.\nYour opponent picks it up just to block you.\nResult: You're denied a 14-point card, and they now hold a dangerous penalty card (14 points if they're not in Spades).",
                },
              },
              {
                type: 'highlight',
                text: 'Watching an opponent pick up the Ace you desperately need is a special kind of pain.',
                emphasis: true,
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Advanced Tactics',
            subtitle: 'For experienced players',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'strategy-block',
                title: '👑 The Kingmaker',
                description: 'In a 4-player game where Player A has an unbeatable hand, Player D (with no chance of winning) can decide who loses the most. By strategically picking up or declining cards, they can sabotage one opponent to help another, effectively choosing second place.',
                example: {
                  type: 'example',
                  text: "This isn't a flaw; it's a feature. It's a core part of the psychological warfare in multiplayer games.",
                },
              },
              {
                type: 'strategy-block',
                title: '🔗 Information Cascade',
                description: "Player A declares Spades. The A♠ appears. Player C (who doesn't need Spades) picks it up just to block Player A.",
                example: {
                  type: 'example',
                  title: 'The Consequence',
                  text: 'Player C now has a powerful penalty card (14 points) in hand, significantly increasing their own risk.\nThe Dilemma: "Do I hurt my opponent now at the cost of hurting myself more later?" The act of blocking is itself a risk.',
                },
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Degenerate Strategies',
            subtitle: "When winning isn't the goal",
            content: [
              {
                type: 'strategy-block',
                title: '😈 The Passive Aggressor',
                description: "A controversial strategy where a player's goal is not to win, but to ensure another specific player loses. This player:",
                example: {
                  type: 'example',
                  text: "Never declares a suit\nPicks up every card of their target's suit\nAccumulates a massive negative score\nSuccessfully torpedoes their rival's game",
                },
              },
              {
                type: 'highlight',
                text: "Warning: This will make you very unpopular at game night. But in high-stakes games or grudge matches, it's a legitimate (if brutal) tactic.",
                emphasis: true,
              },
              {
                type: 'highlight',
                text: "CLAIM is more than a game of cards; it's a game of people. Politics, alliances, and rivalries all come into play.",
                emphasis: true,
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
